; Ozbound level data: Bluebrook, the vertical-slice world (meadow, village, forest).
;
; Same format as assets/maps/meadow.map, plus optional sections for the village slice.
; Lines starting with ';' are comments. Blank lines are ignored. Sections may appear in any
; order, each at most once. Required:
; Geography (64 x 40 tiles): a meadow with a heron pond in the west, a river at x = 26-27 crossed
; by the wooden bridge on the main road (y = 20), and the village of Bluebrook east of the river:
; three widely spaced plots (the apothecary's physic garden to the north, the surveyor's kitchen
; garden to the north-east, the woodcutter's vineyard to the south-east), each with a roomy
; house, joined to the road by short paths. A forest closes the edges. The road runs on through
; the map's east edge (x = 63, y = 20) and continues as the Yellow Brick Road: the next region is
; placed against that edge in the overworld, so the walk never stops for a loading screen.

[map]
; '.' grass, '=' path, '~' water, 'T' tree, '#' rock, 'F' fence, 'S' signpost,
; 'g' garden bed, 'v' vineyard row (both block movement; walk the grass lanes between).
; Houses are not drawn here: the [houses] section stamps walls, a doorway, and floor.
